  "surprise": "P30 head-wise gated attention (Qiu et al. 2025; sigmoid(Linear(384, 8)(ln1(x))) on the SDPA output before proj in all six Peri-LN blocks, zero-init, AdamW; 9,576,240 params as registered) on 153-claude scored 634/635/639 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 636.00 vs 687.00, -51.00, paired -42/-65/-46, every seed down and below the registered -30..+35 range. Discard. The mechanism was ACTIVE, so this is a real negative, not a null: on 400 held-out records the seed-0 pretrain.pt gates are far from uniform (block 0's four NoPE heads have per-token gate std 0.30-0.38 with 11% of values < 0.1 and 14% > 0.9, i.e. they learned a per-token off switch as hypothesized; block 2 head 2 (ALiBi slope 1/64) sits at mean 0.21; head means range 0.19-0.86), and RL left them almost unchanged (final.pt gate weight RMS 0.027-0.033 vs 0.026-0.033, head means shift <= 0.15). Pretraining loss went the right way and RL did not: final main val 0.0854/0.0781/0.0760 (153: 0.0883/0.0869/0.0888), minima 0.0757/0.0772/0.0755 at 180/225/105 s, but held-out greedy fell slightly (0.957/0.9655/0.9605 vs 0.9675/0.967/0.968) and the T=0.8 sampler was clearly worse at the start of expert iteration: round-1 targets solved 591/764/602 (mean 652 vs 153's 766/747/694 = 736, sample acc 0.182/0.280/0.182 vs ~0.27), the registered 650-820 range missed on two seeds; round-4 RL-solved 1112/1129/1134 (153: 1157) recovered most of the gap but the transfer eval did not (by-bin: length 7 at 0.58-0.62, 10 at 0.34-0.35). Speed sub-prediction missed low: 4162/4168/4139 steps (mean 4156 vs 4503, -7.7%, below the registered 4,200-4,650 on every seed; the < 4,000 falsifier did not fire), 3.68 epochs, so the sigmoid/transpose/multiply and their backward over 7 blocks cost more launches than the ~1% estimated; RL sampling 205-293 samples/s, totals 1647/1792/1633 s. Pattern: like 152 (drop-path), 155 (low-rank bigram) and 157 (curriculum, trigram) a change that matches or improves the pretraining loss made a worse T=0.8 sampler for round 1, and the metric follows round 1. 159-fable3 registered the elementwise variant of the same P30 idea (Linear(384,384) gate paid by d_ff 1280 -> 1088) two seconds before this run; the pair separates head-wise from element-wise gating on the same incumbent.",
